        "reason": "Carrier A (authenticate): command that changes system state (DB write for last_login, token generation, user record mutation). Carrier B (refresh): query that returns new token but has NO side effects (pure function). Carrier C (validate): query that only reads/decodes token, returns metadata, NO side effects. Unifying these into one method would create a VIOLATION of Command-Query Separation — callers expect either state change OR read-only result, not both. This is a CATASTROPHIC anti-pattern."
